1
00:00:00,175 --> 00:00:03,870
Hang one weight on a spring, it stretches. Double the weight—it stretches twice as far!

2
00:00:04,575 --> 00:00:06,653
Scrambled Latin letters, Hooke? Explain your hidden law!

3
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:09,268
More stretch means more pullback—F equals minus k x!

4
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:14,986
Next, Hooke aimed his brass microscope at cork—and named those tiny honeycomb rooms 'cells'!

5
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:18,257
Warning: stretch past the elastic limit, and metal deforms forever.

6
00:00:18,572 --> 00:00:20,235
No! You snapped my watch spring!

7
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:24,996
Yet Hooke's tiny spiral hairspring tamed the pocket watch—shrinking clocks to fit your palm!

8
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:29,218
Car shocks, skyscrapers, even DNA coils today—all obey Robert Hooke's law.
